#
# Conformance case: paraconsistency/within-world-glut-isolated
# AC: paraconsistency — the SAME contradictory pair as within-world-glut, but split
# across two worlds, stays ISOLATED (each world `consistent`, no explosion).
#
# This is the explicit CONTRAST partner of paraconsistency/within-world-glut: the two
# cases carry the identical contradictory data (CrimePenalty classified both Strict and
# Lenient, those two disjoint) and differ ONLY in graph placement —
#
#   * within-world-glut         : both type-assertions in ONE world  => `inconsistent`
#                                 (the glut is within-world; the witness is captured).
#   * within-world-glut-isolated: the two type-assertions in SEPARATE worlds => each
#                                 world `consistent` (the disjointness never co-occurs
#                                 with both memberships in one world, so no owl:Nothing
#                                 clash fires; the contradiction is confined per-world).
#
# Together the pair makes the Paraconsistency invariant machine-checked from BOTH sides:
# a within-world contradiction emits a captured witness, while the same contradiction
# isolated across worlds does not contaminate either world (cross-world coexistence,
# mirroring paraconsistency/cross-world-isolation). The behavioral distinction is
# decided by world placement, GENUINELY by the native DL consistency path
# (gmeow_logic::reason::dl_consistency), and diffed against expected/verdicts.json.
#
# verdict_mode=consistency: the OWL EDB is the world-scoped N-Quads in input.nq; this
# file exists only to satisfy the per-case anatomy and is NOT compiled.
@prefix logic: <https://blackcatinformatics.ca/logic/> .
